gn policy for decades at  this point since In 1902 it had signed a  secret treaty with France they agreed  that the two would never go to war with  the other in return for them respecting  each other's fears of influence in North  Africa which is why when the first world  war broke out Italy declared itself  neutral this wasn't to say it had closed  the door to Austria-Hungary in Germany  forever though its foreign policy in  1914 was dictated by one question who  can give Italy the most Germany offered  Italy this from France if it ended the  war whereas is Austria-Hungary was less  keen on Italy joining the war properly  and so offered some of its own lands to  Italy on the condition that it stayed  neutral and gave some trade concessions  whereas the Anton offered Italy all of  this a promise that it would 100 honor  after the war Italy much preferred what  Britain and France was offering and so  it signed the Treaty of London agreeing  to Wade the entente which surely meant  that Italian entry against the Central  Powers was guaranteed right well no  Antonio solandra was the Prime Minister  of Italy in 1915 but his position was  very fragile and Italy itself was  politically very divided with most  people much preferring neutrality this  wasn't out of some deep Italian love for  the Central Powers but because War sucks  and you can make a lot of money trading  with Warring States anyway salandra was  fiercely pro-ontaunt whereas the last  prime minister in salandra's main  opponent Giovanni gioletti was  pro-central Powers when the writing  looked to be on the wall gieliti met  with the German Chancellor to arrange  what he could do if he replaced salandra  knowing that if he did nothing he would  lose his job solandra did the only thing  he could he quit he did this not because  he actually wanted to to quit because he  knew that Parliament wouldn't back him  and by quitting he forced the king to  choose if the king let him resign then  the king backed the Central Powers if  the king refused to accept his  resignation then it meant to be back the  on taunt he knew that Parliament would  never act against the king's wishes at  such a time and so when the king ordered  salandra to stay in office his position  was Secure and thus Italy was free to  join the war alongside France and  Britain which he did in May 1915. I hope  you enjoyed this episode with the  special thanks to my patreon supporters  James bisonet Kelly moneymaker Sky  Chappelle call show wolf kotoitska  Adam's daughter Jerry lambdin Alex  Schwinn Jordan Longley Marcus Arsenal  rod D Martin wyan hockey Spencer  Lightfoot Captain psydog Marvin Castle  boogly Wiggly kimun Yoon Winston K wood  Aaron the white the mcwhopper Miss izet  Maggie paxkowski Gustav Swan Anthony  Beckett Coppertone shewenin spinning  three plates Charles the first and words  about books podcast
 

